# This file provides an example origin allow-list for the orchestrator (--origins)
# Using this file, the orchestrator can enforce the available addresses/protocols a CLI may use in measurements
# A measurement is refused unless every origin it uses matches a rule below
# src_addr is an anycast IP address, or 'unicastv4'/'unicastv6' (each worker's local unicast address)
# The protocol list may be 'all' to allow all protocols (icmp, dns, tcp, chaos)
# src_addr, protocol[, protocol...]
10.0.0.1, all
2001:db8::1, icmp, tcp
unicastv4, icmp
unicastv6, icmp
